# Hunt passive animals until n food items are held. The hunting half of
# `get_food`, split out so `get_food` can first leave a shelter and still keep
# the core's six-rule limit (run 9, third review): a body sealed in at night
# whose food bar turned critical used to start hunting from inside the
# shelter, find nothing, fail, and stay sealed.
#
# Why the rules are ordered this way: the goal check is on top, so the skill
# also works on its own. Then the animal that is in sight is hunted, cow first
# (the most meat), then pig, sheep and chicken; `hunt` ends by itself when the
# kill and the pickup are done, and this skill looks again. Raw meat counts as
# food: `eat_food` eats whatever the arbiter chooses, and cooking (`cook_food`)
# is a separate goal because it needs a furnace. With no animal in sight the
# body explores for a cow; an animal that comes into sight on the way is
# hunted on the next tick, because every tick starts at the top. `explore` ends
# when a cow is within 24 blocks; a failed search ends the skill `not_found`
# after the usual three tries, and the caller decides what then.
skill hunt_food(n: int = 2)
  doc "Have n food items: hunt cows, pigs, sheep and chickens in sight (else explore for a cow) and pick up the meat."
  rules:
    count_food() >= $n -> done
    near_entity(cow, 24) -> do hunt(cow, beef)
    near_entity(pig, 24) -> do hunt(pig, porkchop)
    near_entity(sheep, 24) -> do hunt(sheep, mutton)
    near_entity(chicken, 24) -> do hunt(chicken, chicken)
    true -> explore(cow)
